       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is well above labeled maximums.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily = 6400 mg/day.**\n\n- The FDA-labeled maximum is 3200 mg/day, so this is double that.\n- 1600 mg per dose is also above the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg for prescription use.\n- At this level, the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, fluid retention, and cardiovascular events. Those risks are higher in older adults, and the patient is 70.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n1. **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours** (max 3200 mg/day), which is the usual range for pain or fever.\n2. **1600 mg PO four times daily** as written, if you have a specific indication and have weighed these risks. I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale.\n3. A different dose or frequency.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
